  <subsection title="Solve Equations with Decimals">
    <p>In previous chapters, we solved equations using the Properties of Equality. We will use these same properties to solve equations with decimals.</p>
    <note type="Properties of Equality">
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Subtraction Property of EqualityFor any numbers $$a,b,\ \text{and}\ c,$$If $$a = b,$$ then $$a - c = b - c.$$</cell>
            <cell>Addition Property of Equality
For any numbers $$a,b,\ \text{and}\ c,$$If $$a = b,$$ then $$a + c = b + c.$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>The Division Property of Equality
For any numbers $$a,b,\ \text{and}\ c,\ \text{and}\ c \neq 0$$If $$a = b,$$ then $$\frac{a}{c} = \frac{b}{c}$$</cell>
            <cell>The Multiplication Property of Equality
For any numbers $$a,b,\ \text{and}\ c,$$If $$a = b,$$ then $$ac = bc$$</cell>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </note>
    <p>When you add, subtract, multiply or divide the same quantity from both sides of an equation, you still have equality.</p>
    <example number="5.41">
      <problem>
        <p>Solve: $$y + 2.3 = -4.7.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>We will use the Subtraction Property of Equality to isolate the variable.</p>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check:</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Since $$y = -7$$ makes $$y + 2.3 = -4.7$$ a true statement, we know we have found a solution to this equation.</p>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.81">
      <p>Solve: $$y + 2.7 = -5.3.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.82">
      <p>Solve: $$y + 3.6 = -4.8.$$</p>
