    <example number="5.42">
      <problem>
        <p>Solve: $$a - 4.75 = -1.39.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>We will use the Addition Property of Equality.</p>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Add 4.75 to each side, to undo the subtraction.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check:</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Since the result is a true statement, $$a = 3.36$$ is a solution to the equation.</p>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.83">
