    <example number="5.43">
      <problem>
        <p>Solve: $$-4.8 = 0.8n.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>We will use the Division Property of Equality.</p>
        <p>Use the Properties of Equality to find a value for $$n.$$</p>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>We must divide both sides by 0.8 to isolate n.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check:</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Since $$n = -6$$ makes $$-4.8 = 0.8n$$ a true statement, we know we have a solution.</p>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.85">
