    <example number="5.44">
      <problem>
        <p>Solve: $$\frac{p}{- 1.8} = -6.5.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>We will use the Multiplication Property of Equality.</p>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Here, p is divided by −1.8. We must multiply by −1.8 to isolate p</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check:</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>A solution to $$\frac{p}{-1.8} = -6.5$$ is $$p = 11.7.$$</p>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.87">
